Orin leafed through a magazine at Pine Creek Dental. His tooth was throbbing, which made it difficult to concentrate. Scientific American had detailed how Breakthrough Starshot (a project funded to the tune of $100M by billionaire Yuri Milner in 2016), had gone bust. Orin knew all too well the pain of having aspirations beyond his means. Although in Orin's case, the limit seemed to be $100K instead of $100M.

After working for 20 years, Orin had about $500K in his 401K - not enough to retire on yet. But, Orin had also managed to string together a series of savvy Crypto investments. In 2013, he wired $1K to Japan and bought 10 Bitcoin when it was worth $100. Somehow, he had even managed to transfer his funds to a cold storage wallet before Mt. Gox imploded. A few years later, he purchased 2,000 ETH at pre-sale (for a grand total of $700). On a whim, he had purchased 4M dogecoin when it was $0.001 each. All told, he had spent $5700 on Crypto.

He was now sitting on $6.7M. The returns were, honestly, a little surreal. His phone (which held his Dogecoin wallet) was worth $1M - sometimes he felt like it was burning a literal hole in his pocket. He knew it was a bad idea to walk around with that much money, but he also didn't want to be tempted to sell it.

After reading about how even $100M could be squandered, Orin decided to continue holding. His toothache had nothing to do with it.October 9, 2025
---------------

The dentist had diagnosed Orin's toothache as sinus pressure and sent him home without a fix. Ibuprofen would have to suffice, it seemed. He didn't mind, really. Pain was just "weakness leaving the body", or so his high school gym teacher had thought. Orin thought it was somewhat sad (yet funny) that he was sitting on $7M and still had such a mundane problem.

He had missed the NVidia boom, despite witnessing the moment that the original TNT graphics card eclipsed 3dfx back in 1998. Between 2000 and 2007, NVDA split three times for a combined 12x multiplier. It didn't split again until 2021, when it split 4:1. And then again in 2024 at 10:1.

For anyone paying attention to the AI boom that started in 2015, NVidia was an easy strategy. Orin should have been paying attention. Instead, he had been playing Starcraft II. Oops.October 10, 2025
