"Cooperative Exponentialism helps us weather the storms of change."
"CE elevates group behavior from the invisible hand to the visible hand."
"Cooperations act where corporations fail."

Orin was experimenting with different taglines for his imaginary company, Cooperation Alpha. A traditional 100K-person corportion with a 6-tier org structure needed 20% overhead just to run the business. Cooperations were wildly different: they only needed a core team of 10 hyper-connected managers who used BCIs to scale their ability to supports workers on a 1:1 basis. They would be far more effective than AI-driven organizations - able to think and adapt in real-time.

A typical company might allocate 15-30% of revenue to a staff budget. Cooperations are able to boost profitability anywhere from 3% to 6% (by eliminating middle management entirely).

