It was too late to eat the hotel's free buffet, but 11AM in Vegas was practically mid afternoon, since the bars never closed. Orin scanned the hotel's ads for brunch. Backstage Deli seemed right up their alley: cheap and open 24/7. He left a note on the table in case Helen woke up, and walked down to the deli.

"Two Sausage Bagel sandiwches, a large order of tots, and two large coffees, please." Orin's blood shot eyes added up the total: $48 for breakfast. Not the worst deal, but easily double the cost of McDonalds. I'm on vacation, Orin thought to himself.

...

