Orin hadn't told Helen they were rich yet. As they boarded the plane back to Omaha, he thought about how best to explain that cryptocurrency had given them the freedom to really chase their dreams. He had read about many lottery winners who squandered their winnings. He didn't want to wind up like the billionaire who had spent $100M with nothing to show for it, either.

"Helen...I've been meaning to tell you something." Orin realized his wording was bad the moment the words left his mouth. Helen's face stiffened.

"Uh...ok." She pursed her lips and looked extremely worried.

"Nothing bad, I swear!" Orin smiled and chuckled at his lack of tact. Internally, he was panicking. Outwardly, his smile seemed to do the trick. Whew.

"OK, so here's the thing. I uh, well look at my phone." Orin handed Helen his Dogecoin app showing an $800K balance.

"What. The. Fuck!" Helen's eyes went wide with shock. "How...did you manage..." Her voice trailed off.

"There's more, actually. That's only about 10% of it." Orin was actually quite proud of himself. He had not realized a public space like an airport might not be the best place to advertise that his phone was burning a hole in his pocket...

"OH! I get it, this is just in your silly game isn't it?" Helen's eyes pleaded with Orin to avoid making them a target.

"Yeah. Haha! Pretty good gag, huh?" Orin really felt sheepish. It seemed to sell the lie to the guy eavesdropping their conversation to Helen's left. Ugh, what good was being rich if you couldn't flaunt it!October 16, 2025
