------------
The key turned softly, though no lock was visible. What opened was a hinge in time, a pivot between banter and burden. Orin stood at the threshold, half-skeptic, half-pilgrim. Joan's words pressed like a seal into wax: revelation, already moving, already chosen. The Arc did not wait for readiness; it only waited for recognition. December flickered ahead, a summons of becoming.